# `peek` reads the program's own source as data.
#
# Zone 0 reads the character at offset 1 of zone 1's body -- the digit `7` -- and
# prints its character code, 55. Then zone 1 runs normally and prints 7. The very
# same `7` is seen two ways: as source text (code 55) and as executed code (7).
{stack 1 1 peek .}
{stack 7 .}
